redit and other insurance products; and vehicle protection, commercial equipment protection, and other related services. The Global Housing segment provides lender-placed homeowners, manufactured housing, and flood insurance; renters insurance and other products; and voluntary manufactured housing, and condominium and homeowners insurance products. The company was formerly known as Fortis, Inc. and changed its name to Assurant, Inc. in February 2004. Assurant, Inc. was founded in 1892 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Keith Warner Demmings | President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $5.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 14K people. Revenue per employee of $866K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $108K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Assurant, Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $15.8B market cap on $12.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 25% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 17-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $1.6B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 12 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.10\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 10.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 20% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7656294768208142},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $12.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 36% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","21 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Are Air New Zealand's (ASX:AIZ) Mobile Plans a New Revenue Lane?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/consumer/are-air-new-zealands-asxaiz-mobile-plans-a-new-revenue-lane","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794457200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why Assurant (AIZ) Might be Well Poised for a Surge","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/why-assurant-aiz-might-well-162002800.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794414002.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.827,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Assurant Continues Commitment to Wounded Veterans with Sixth Mobility-Modified Vehicle","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/assurant-continues-commitment-wounded-veterans-140000549.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794405600.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.922,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Can LMND's Nationwide Renters Insurance Expansion Accelerate Growth?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/real-estate/articles/lmnds-nationwide-renters-insurance-expansion-171900222.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794590340.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.736,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Are Smaller ASX 300 Names Sending A Warning Signal This November?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/smallcap/are-smaller-asx-300-names-sending-a-warning-signal-this-november","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794546480.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.226,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tag